    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1579">

                <pb facs="1166" n="1050" xml:id="pg1050"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.5212/1a.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Brazilian Minister to
                        Mexico</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-02-03">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>431. Department informed by Spanish Embassy here that Angel Caso, Special
                    Representative of Spanish Government near General Villa, now in Mexico City,
                    threatened with arrest by Carranza forces.</p>
                <p>Please confer with appropriate authorities and point out to them the serious
                    consequences that may result from the arrest of a diplomatic officer of a
                    foreign government and strenuously protest against such action. Mr. Silliman may
                    be of service in matter in view of his friendly relations with General
                    Carranza.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
